.Sh DESCRIPTION
Copy Gum modules into a project.
Gum is the set of optional Wattle modules installed in
.Ql "share/wattle/src/gum"
under
.Ql "*prefix*" .
.Ic g
is a synonym for
.Cm gum .
.Pp
With no
.Ar module ,
.Cm gum
prints the name and a description of each module in two columns,
wrapped as
.Fl "-help"
wraps.
With one or more,
it copies the files of each,
which are its source and its licence,
into the
.Ql "gum"
directory of
.Ar directory ,
and prints
.Ql "copied"
or
.Ql "unchanged"
and the path of each file.
A project imports a copy by its path,
as in
.Ql "\*(lpimport \&./deps/gum/args :as args\*(rp" .
A build made without the OS library does not include
.Cm gum ,
and it exits with status 1 after saying so.
.Pp
.Cm gum
checks every
.Ar module
and every destination before it copies a file.
It exits with status 1 having copied nothing if a
.Ar module
is not one of Gum’s,
or if a destination file exists with content that differs from
its source.
A file with the same content is left as it is.
.
